  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>La Corderie is a Mediterranean restaurant at 20 quai de la Corderie, on the Port de la Darse in Villefranche-sur-Mer. Its website presents it as one of the last authentic corners of the Côte d'Azur: a sunny terrace covered by an imposing plane tree, facing the boats and the clinking of their masts, with modern Mediterranean cuisine with a Provençal accent, at lunch and dinner. The tourist office adds that it relies on local fishing and seasonal produce.</p>

      <h2>At the table</h2>
      <p>The à la carte menu runs from €15 to €35, group menus from €35 to €75. Bouillabaisse, the house speciality, must be ordered 48 hours ahead by phone (not on Sundays): €80 per person, for 2 to 30 people. A petanque court on the terrace is available to all customers during opening hours. The restaurant has 100 seats on the terrace and 50 indoors (two rooms, one air-conditioned). It has no car park, offers a baby chair and is wheelchair accessible with help. Bank cards, cash, American Express and meal vouchers are accepted.</p>

      <h2>Opening hours</h2>
      <p>The tourist office announces opening every day, from 11am to 3pm and from 6pm to 10:30pm, with closure on the evenings of 24 and 31 December. It also states: open every day for lunch and dinner except Wednesday and Thursday evenings, and every day, evenings included, from April to September. Phone: 04 93 76 61 31.</p>

      <h2>What about the dog?</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's listing on the Nice Côte d'Azur tourist office website says "Animals accepted" and "Animals are accepted". It does not specify whether dogs are admitted indoors as well as on the terrace, nor whether there is a size limit or a surcharge. The restaurant's website does not cover the subject.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book a table on the terrace, under the plane tree, and bring a water bowl for your dog, as the sun beats down on the harbour in summer.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant faces the Port de la Darse. Other tables on the Port de la Darse appear in the tourist office's practical guide, for example La Baleine Joyeuse and La Stoa (Hôtel de la Darse), to vary or extend the walk by the water with your dog.</p>
